UID:pulitzer-center-global-south-civil-society-microgrants-2026@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pulitzer Center: Global South Civil Society Microgrants 2
 026
DESCRIPTION:The Pulitzer Center funds civil society in the Global South to 
 build civic engagement projects around Pulitzer Center-supported journalis
 m: grassroots collectives\, community-led movements\, ARTISTS and civic co
 alitions taking published reporting to the communities it concerns. This g
 rant cycle is restricted to the Center's Climate and Environment topics: R
 AINFOREST (drivers of rainforest degradation\, the role of global markets\
 , finance and policy\, centring the rights and roles of Indigenous peoples
 )\, OCEAN (degradation of marine environments\, ocean health and the clima
 te crisis\, ocean governance\, science-backed and community-led solutions)
 \, and CLIMATE AND LABOR (the intersection of climate and labour\, includi
 ng gender\, livelihoods\, adaptation and community resilience). WHAT COUNT
 S AS A PROJECT: community engagement and organising that connects reportin
 g with audiences\; creative expressions\, explicitly including digital cam
 paigns\, public performances and creative publication formats\; public dia
 logues bringing together affected communities\, journalists\, decision-mak
 ers and academia\; and other innovative uses of the reporting that build o
 n local cultural practices. Every project must use at least one published 
 Pulitzer Center-supported reporting project meaningfully\, or involve a Pu
 litzer Center-supported journalist centrally\, and must name a clear targe
 t audience. OUT OF SCOPE: journalism and reporting projects themselves (th
 ose go to the Center's reporting grants)\, anything not built on Pulitzer 
 Center-supported reporting\, direct advocacy or lobbying\, campaigns endor
 sing political candidates or parties\, and for-profit projects. WHO CAN AP
 PLY: grassroots organisations\, community educators\, civil society organi
 sations and coalitions\, youth movements and other groups working at the i
 ntersection of journalism\, civic rights and active citizenship\, with pas
 t experience running civic engagement activities in the Global South\, pro
 ven experience on the named topics\, and the operational capacity to manag
 e a microgrant from an international organisation. APPLICATION: a project 
 description of no more than 400 words\, the target audience and desired im
 pact\, your methodology\, a timeline and budget\, the lead applicant's CV 
 with a letter of recommendation\, and\, where activities involve Indigenou
 s peoples or traditional communities\, a signed or recorded statement of c
 onsent from a community member. Applications are accepted in English\, Spa
 nish\, Portuguese\, French and Indonesian through Submittable. TIMELINE: a
 pplications 15 August to 6 September 2026\, selection announced mid-Septem
 ber 2026\, onboarding October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Pulitzer Center\nLoca
 tion: Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and South
 east Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. Ci
 vil Society Microgrant instead.\nAward: USD 2\,000 to USD 4\,000 per proje
 ct. Applicants name the amount requested and submit a draft budget. Funds 
 are transferred to the partner after the agreement is signed\; partners fi
 le a financial narrative and outcomes report at the end but are NOT requir
 ed to collect detailed receipts. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to six 
 months of implementation\, October 2026 to March 2027\, with a virtual che
 ck-in in December 2026 and closure in early March 2027.\n\nMore: https://p
 ulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/global-south-
 civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://pulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/g
 lobal-south-civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and Sou
 theast Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. 
 Civil Society Microgrant instead.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:asian-cultural-council-individual-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council: Individual Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's Individual Fellowship funds artist
 s\, scholars and arts professionals from Asia and the U.S. to spend one to
  six months somewhere new or less familiar\, pursuing self-designed resear
 ch and cultural immersion: meeting practitioners\, visiting studios\, muse
 ums\, galleries\, theatres and libraries\, joining workshops and symposia\
 , and doing archival research. ACC is explicit that this is not a producti
 on residency\, not a conference travel grant and not a PR tour. APPLYING J
 OINTLY: two or three people who share research goals can apply together as
  equal partners (one primary applicant\, up to two co-applicants\, no assi
 stant roles)\; the USD 35\,000 cap covers the whole team. Applicants must 
 be citizens or legal permanent residents of an ACC-eligible country\, terr
 itory or region: Afghanistan\, Bangladesh\, Bhutan\, Brunei\, Cambodia\, C
 hina (Mainland)\, East Timor\, Hong Kong SAR\, India\, Indonesia\, Japan\,
  Korea\, Laos\, Macau SAR\, Malaysia\, Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakist
 an\, Philippines\, Singapore\, Sri Lanka\, Taiwan\, Thailand\, the U.S. an
 d Vietnam. ELIGIBLE DISCIPLINES (16): architecture (design\, history and t
 heory)\, archaeology\, art history\, arts administration\, arts criticism\
 , conservation\, crafts\, curation\, dance\, ethnomusicology\, film\, lite
 rature\, museum studies\, music\, theater and visual art\; video art and p
 hotography apply under visual art. Additional requirements: at least 21 ye
 ars old by the start\, at least five years of professional experience in a
 n eligible discipline\, no university coursework or teaching during the fe
 llowship\, and confident English if travelling to the U.S. on a J-1 visa. 
 Anyone who has held an ACC grant in the last two calendar years is ineligi
 ble. DESTINATIONS: any eligible country except the one you currently live 
 in\; a place you have lived in for over a year or hold citizenship in need
 s a strong rationale. U.S. fellowships need at least 30 consecutive days a
 nd cannot start before 1 October 2027 because of J-1 processing\; fellowsh
 ips in Asia need 30 cumulative days\, splittable into trips of at least 14
  consecutive days with no more than 14 days between them. ACC sponsors the
  J-1 for U.S. travel\; for Asia you arrange your own visas\, and the fees 
 can go in the budget. WHAT ACC WILL NOT FUND: this is strictly cultural-ex
 change and immersion funding\, not production money. Filming a documentary
 \, researching a planned book or film\, mounting an exhibition\, running a
  concert series\, promotional or PR travel\, equipment purchases and full-
 time residency programmes are all ineligible\, as is funding used only to 
 travel to a single event. TIMELINE: the portal opens 1 October 2026 at 9:5
 9am ET\, applications close 10 November 2026 at 9:59am ET\, and letters of
  recommendation are due 16 November 2026 at 9:59am ET. Review runs Novembe
 r 2026 to April 2027\, notifications go out mid-May 2027\, and all funded 
 activity must take place between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2028. Apply
  through the GoApply portal\; ACC does not accept email applications. Appl
 icants may apply to only one ACC programme per cycle. No application fee.\
 n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council (ACC)\nLocation: Travel between an
 d within Asia and the United States. Open to citizens and legal permanent 
 residents of ACC-eligible countries\, territories and regions\, including 
 the U.S. You cannot propose travel to the place where you currently live.\
 nAward: Up to USD 35\,000\, the same cap whether you apply alone or jointl
 y with up to two co-applicants. Covers economy airfare\, ground transport\
 , accommodation\, food and daily living costs\, visa fees\, mandatory trav
 el health insurance\, interpretation and costs tied to the exchange activi
 ties. Also included: ACC logistical and research guidance\, introductions 
 to alumni and professionals\, and visa assistance for U.S. travel. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: One to six months\, at least 30 days in the destin
 ation\; ACC prefers two months or more in a single place.\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Travel between and within Asia and the United States. Open to citi
 zens and legal permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries\, territories
  and regions\, including the U.S. You cannot propose travel to the place w
 here you currently live.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:asian-cultural-council-organization-grant-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council: Organization Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:ACC's Organization Grant funds arts and culture organisations i
 n Asia and the U.S. to run cultural-exchange activities for their staff\, 
 communities and collaborators: sending an activity lead and participants a
 broad\, hosting incoming participants at home\, or both. Up to USD 50\,000
 \, set by ACC against the proposed budget\, activities\, travel duration a
 nd application quality. ELIGIBILITY: the applicant must be a nonprofit\, a
  government-affiliated or sponsored arts or cultural institution (national
  museums\, performing arts centres and the like)\, or an academic or highe
 r-education institution\; legally registered and based in an ACC-eligible 
 country\, territory or region\; and have at least five years of artistic o
 r cultural programming experience. Each application names a primary contac
 t\, an activity lead who runs the work on the ground (can be the same pers
 on)\, and activity participants who may be staff or external collaborators
 . The lead and all participants must be citizens or legal permanent reside
 nts of an eligible location\, and they do not have to share a nationality 
 with each other or with the organisation. Applicants must be citizens or l
 egal permanent residents of an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region:
  Afghanistan\, Bangladesh\, Bhutan\, Brunei\, Cambodia\, China (Mainland)\
 , East Timor\, Hong Kong SAR\, India\, Indonesia\, Japan\, Korea\, Laos\, 
 Macau SAR\, Malaysia\, Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakistan\, Philippines
 \, Singapore\, Sri Lanka\, Taiwan\, Thailand\, the U.S. and Vietnam. ELIGI
 BLE DISCIPLINES (16): architecture (design\, history and theory)\, archaeo
 logy\, art history\, arts administration\, arts criticism\, conservation\,
  crafts\, curation\, dance\, ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum 
 studies\, music\, theater and visual art\; video art and photography apply
  under visual art. TRAVEL: one to six months within the grant period\, at 
 least 30 consecutive days in the U.S. or 30 cumulative days in Asia (split
 table into trips of at least 14 consecutive days\, no more than 14 days ap
 art). Travel to a place the lead or participants have spent over a year in
  needs a strong rationale\, and multi-destination or short itineraries are
  less competitive. ACC does not sponsor visas for this programme\; the org
 anisation secures them. WHAT ACC WILL NOT FUND: this is strictly cultural-
 exchange and immersion funding\, not production money. Filming a documenta
 ry\, researching a planned book or film\, mounting an exhibition\, running
  a concert series\, promotional or PR travel\, equipment purchases and ful
 l-time residency programmes are all ineligible\, as is funding used only t
 o travel to a single event. TIMELINE: the portal opens 1 October 2026 at 9
 :59am ET\, applications close 10 November 2026 at 9:59am ET\, and letters 
 of recommendation are due 16 November 2026 at 9:59am ET. Review runs Novem
 ber 2026 to April 2027\, notifications go out mid-May 2027\, and all funde
 d activity must take place between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2028. App
 ly through the GoApply portal\; ACC does not accept email applications. Ap
 plicants may apply to only one ACC programme per cycle. No application fee
 .\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council (ACC)\nLocation: Asia and the Un
 ited States. The applicant organisation must be legally registered and bas
 ed in an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region\; activity leads and p
 articipants must be citizens or permanent residents of an eligible locatio
 n\, not necessarily the same one as the organisation.\nAward: Up to USD 50
 \,000. Covers economy airfare\, ground transport\, accommodation\, food an
 d daily living costs\, visa fees\, mandatory travel health insurance\, int
 erpretation and costs tied to the exchange activities. Also included: ACC 
 logistical and substantive guidance\, introductions to alumni\, arts profe
 ssionals and institutions\, and invitations to local ACC events. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: One to six months of travel\; at least 30 consecutiv
 e days for U.S. activity\, or 30 cumulative days in Asia.\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Asia and the United States. The applicant organisation must be leg
 ally registered and based in an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region
 \; activity leads and participants must be citizens or permanent residents
  of an eligible location\, not necessarily the same one as the organisatio
 n.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:design-trust-seed-feature-impact-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:Deadline: Design Trust Seed\, Feature & Impact Grants (Hong Kong / 
 Greater Bay Area)
DESCRIPTION:Design Trust offers grants to individual designers\, curators\,
  collectives\, and non-profit organisations for projects and activities re
 levant to various design disciplines\, supporting work relevant to the con
 text and content of Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area (the Special Admini
 strative Regions of Hong Kong and Macao and the nine Guangdong municipalit
 ies of Guangzhou\, Shenzhen\, Zhuhai\, Foshan\, Huizhou\, Dongguan\, Zhong
 shan\, Jiangmen\, and Zhaoqing). It supports innovative\, thought-provokin
 g investigations across design disciplines from graphics\, media\, and wea
 rables to architecture and the built environment\, including exhibitions\,
  research projects\, and creative installations that advocate the positive
  role of design in the region. THREE GRANTS: (1) SEED GRANT (HKD 50\,000) 
 fosters experimentation\, testing\, and sharing\, awarded to individuals k
 ick-starting a meaningful project with social\, educational\, economical\,
  or environmental impact\; supports emerging designers\, young scholars\, 
 and projects in the pipeline needing additional resources\, including rese
 arch and prototypes focused on Hong Kong and Greater Bay Area issues to be
  showcased at international venues\, symposia\, or biennales. (2) FEATURE 
 GRANT (capped at HKD 300\,000\, awarded annually upon special consideratio
 n) fosters cross-disciplinary projects on the Greater Bay Area with wide-r
 eaching audiences\, often sited at an exhibition or biennale of internatio
 nal standing\, supporting exchange between a Hong Kong/China-based collect
 ive and an internationally renowned cultural institution. (3) IMPACT GRANT
  supports public-facing\, community-based projects led by former Design Tr
 ust grant recipients\, fellows\, and mentees with a proven track record\; 
 considered case-by-case (contact grantapplication@designtrust.hk). ELIGIBI
 LITY: individuals\, collectives\, and certified non-profit organisations e
 ither based in the Greater Bay Area or seeking support for design projects
  related to the region. Individuals or collectives who have completed two 
 Feature Grants or three Seed Grants should apply for the Impact Grant inst
 ead. APPLICATION: two cycles annually\, deadlines 20 April and 20 October 
 (late submissions roll to the next cycle)\; apply at least 3 to 6 months b
 efore the project's commencement. Design Trust may provide full or partial
  funding on a case-by-case basis.\n\nOrganisation: Design Trust\nLocation:
  Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area. Open to applicants based in the regio
 n or seeking support for design projects related to it\, including interna
 tional applicants.\nAward: Seed Grant: HKD 50\,000. Feature Grant: capped 
 at HKD 300\,000\, awarded annually upon special consideration. Impact Gran
 t: case-by-case\, for former grantees. Full or partial funding on a case-b
 y-case basis. Free to apply.\nDuration: Two grant cycles annually (deadlin
 es 20 April and 20 October)\; apply 3 to 6 months before project commencem
 ent\n\nMore: https://designtrust.hk/grants/dtgrants/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://designtrust.hk/grants/dtgrants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area. Open to applicants based in th
 e region or seeking support for design projects related to it\, including 
 international applicants.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:india-foundation-arts-research-programme-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Deadline: India Foundation for the Arts: Arts Research Programme (M
 ay 2026 Request for Proposals)
DESCRIPTION:IFA's Arts Research Programme funds research into forms of know
 ing and thinking rooted in creative\, scholarly or cultural practice. It e
 xplicitly welcomes experimental and self-reflexive methodologies\, practic
 e-based inquiry\, interdisciplinary dialogue\, community engagement\, tran
 slation studies and work on marginalised narratives\, with a shareable pub
 lic outcome expected. Open to artists\, scholars\, curators\, translators\
 , educators and practitioner-researchers. ELIGIBILITY IS RESTRICTED: India
 n nationals only\, and PIO and OCI card holders are explicitly excluded\; 
 any collaborators must also be Indian nationals. Applicants need a PAN car
 d and valid ID. PROCESS NOTE: this is a two-stage email application\, not 
 a web form. Applicants were expected to discuss the project concept with t
 he Programme Officer (harshita@indiaifa.org) by 11 July 2026\, with the fi
 nal proposal\, CV and budget breakdown emailed by 10 August 2026 at 23:59 
 IST\, in an email no larger than 25 MB. Proposals may be written in any In
 dian language\, including English.\n\nOrganisation: India Foundation for t
 he Arts (IFA)\nLocation: India\; project-based with no residency requireme
 nt. Open to Indian nationals only.\nAward: Up to INR 500\,000 (around USD 
 5\,700 / EUR 4\,900) per project. Honorarium is capped at 35 percent of th
 e budget. Institutional overhead\, building costs\, infrastructure and equ
 ipment purchases are excluded. No application fee.\nDuration: Minimum 12 m
 onths\, maximum 18 months.\n\nMore: https://indiaifa.org/whats-new/ar-rfp-
 may2026.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://indiaifa.org/whats-new/ar-rfp-may2026.html?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India\; project-based with no residency requirement. Open to India
 n nationals only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inlaks-fine-art-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation: Inlaks Fine Art Award 2027
DESCRIPTION:A one-year award enabling an emerging Indian visual artist to p
 ursue independent practice\, with a stipulation to attend a recognised art
  residency programme in India for four weeks during the year. ELIGIBILITY 
 IS RESTRICTED: Indian citizens currently living in India\, born on or afte
 r 1 January 1996\, who are either recent graduates\, postgraduates or fina
 l-year students of a leading Indian visual arts institute\, or artists wit
 hout those formal credentials but with a record of exhibition participatio
 n. First-year MA students are not eligible. Awardees submit progress repor
 ts at six months and on completion\, plus documentation of the residency. 
 Applications close 15 August 2026 at 23:59 IST via Submittable. Shortlisti
 ng is expected in late October 2026 with interviews in early November.\n\n
 Organisation: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation\nLocation: India. Open to India
 n citizens currently living in India.\nAward: INR 300\,000 (around USD 3\,
 400 / EUR 2\,950) for one year\, plus a fully covered four-week art reside
 ncy at an Indian art institution. No application fee.\nDuration: Twelve mo
 nths of independent practice\, including a mandatory four-week residency w
 ithin India.\n\nMore: https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e1
 4093-df9b-41c5-af96-ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e14093-df9b-41c5-af96
 -ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India. Open to Indian citizens currently living in India.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inlaks-theatre-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation: Inlaks Theatre Art Award 20
 27
DESCRIPTION:A skill-enhancement award for emerging Indian theatre practitio
 ners\, supporting participation in recognised training workshops\, residen
 cies and similar programmes rather than the production of a specific work.
  ELIGIBILITY IS RESTRICTED: Indian citizens born after 1 January 1991\, wi
 th preference given to holders of a theatre degree from a leading Indian i
 nstitution. Recipients report at the six-month mark and on completion. App
 lications close 15 August 2026 at 23:59 IST via Submittable. The foundatio
 n runs several other awards on adjacent deadlines\, including the Inlaks-A
 ttakkalari Dance Studentship (30 August 2026) and a two-month Inlaks Resid
 ency at the International Center of Photography in the USA for emerging In
 dian photographic practitioners (31 August 2026).\n\nOrganisation: Inlaks 
 Shivdasani Foundation\nLocation: India. Open to Indian citizens.\nAward: I
 NR 15\,000 per month for up to 12 months\, around INR 180\,000 total (roug
 hly USD 2\,050 / EUR 1\,780). No application fee.\nDuration: Up to twelve 
 months of skill enhancement\, with six-month interim and final reporting.\
 n\nMore: https://www.inlaksfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.inlaksfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India. Open to Indian citizens.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arm-holding-commission-h-residence-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260726
SUMMARY:Deadline: A.R.M. Holding / Art Dubai Projects: H Residence Sculptur
 e Park Commission (Dubai)
DESCRIPTION:A.R.M. Holding and HUNA\, with the commission supported and man
 aged by Art Dubai Projects\, invite artists to propose a permanent public 
 artwork for the H Residence Sculpture Park in Dubai\, the anchor piece of 
 the park's programme. Artists respond to the theme 'We Emerge Stronger tha
 n Before' through a permanent\, site-specific outdoor sculpture\; the stro
 ngest proposals will find what the phrase opens up (continuity\, endurance
 \, renewal\, collective presence\, the long view) through material\, form\
 , scale and the conditions of the site. Where language or text is incorpor
 ated\, Arabic should lead. TECHNICAL: footprint minimum around 15 sqm\, up
  to 3 m high\; weight restriction 5.5 kN/m2\; must be suitable for long-te
 rm outdoor display in Dubai (summer over 40 C\, humidity to 90 percent\, a
 bout six hours direct sun daily)\; presence by day and night. ELIGIBILITY:
  open to artists with or without gallery representation\; UAE-based\, regi
 onal and international artists welcome\; prior experience with permanent o
 r large-scale outdoor/public installation required. BUDGET: AED 1\,000\,00
 0 all-inclusive\; shortlisted artists receive full budget parameters and p
 roposal fees at the proposal development stage. SUBMISSION: CV and portfol
 io (attention to outdoor\, large-scale or permanent commissions)\, concept
  statement (max 300 words)\, a render or visualisation in context plus at 
 least one sketch\, technical specifications\, and a site response. TIMELIN
 E: submissions close 25 July 2026\; shortlist notified from 10 August\; co
 mmission awarded after September proposal development\; work unveiled at H
  Residence on 2 December 2026. Local fabrication strongly preferred. Quest
 ions: Shahad@artdubai.ae.\n\nOrganisation: A.R.M. Holding / HUNA / Art Dub
 ai Projects\nLocation: H Residence Sculpture Park\, Dubai\, UAE. Open to U
 AE-based\, regional and international artists.\nAward: AED 1\,000\,000 com
 mission envelope\, inclusive of artist fee\, design development\, fabricat
 ion\, materials\, production\, transport\, installation\, lighting and fin
 ishing. Proposal fees are available for shortlisted artists. No submission
  fee.\nDuration: Proposal development September 2026\; fabrication autumn 
 2026\; unveiling 2 December 2026\n\nMore: https://www.artdubai.ae/wp-conte
 nt/uploads/2026/06/ADP_ARM-HOLDING-COMMISSION_OPEN-CALL-PACK-.pdf?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.artdubai.ae/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/ADP_ARM-HOLDING-COMM
 ISSION_OPEN-CALL-PACK-.pdf?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:H Residence Sculpture Park\, Dubai\, UAE. Open to UAE-based\, regi
 onal and international artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-inside-out-art-museum-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T124109Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Inside-Out Art Museum Residency 2027 (Bei
 jing)
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at Inside-Out Art Museu
 m (IOAM) in Beijing\, one of China's leading independent platforms for con
 temporary art and research. The museum combines exhibitions\, critical inq
 uiry and public programmes\, giving residents room for in-depth research\,
  experimentation and exchange within a Chinese art scene that is otherwise
  hard to access from Europe. The residency is framed as cultural exchange 
 rather than production to deadline: IOAM works with a flexible model that 
 takes the resident's other obligations into account and sets the exact sta
 rt date in consultation with the selected candidate. WHO: visual artists\,
  curators and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of th
 e Kingdom. Duos and collaborations may apply (two artists\, two curators/c
 ritics\, or a combination who structurally make work together\, submitting
  a joint plan for the work period that leads to a single result\, and who 
 live and work together in the same space during the residency)\, but each 
 individual must submit a separate application\; the apartment is well suit
 ed to duos or partnerships. WORK PERIOD: one period of three months\, 1 Ma
 rch to 30 May 2027\, with room for one artist or duo\; you can state a pre
 ference for the work period in the application form. Selection is by advis
 ory committee\; read the Mondriaan Fund Residency explanation for the cond
 itions\, assessment and checklist\, plus the fund's general terms and cond
 itions\, before applying. DEADLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00
  Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Insi
 de-Out Art Museum\nLocation: Beijing\, China. For visual artists\, curator
 s and critics based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdo
 m\, funded by the Mondriaan Fund.\nAward: Subsidy of EUR 8\,478 for an art
 ist or EUR 5\,622 for a curator/critic toward travel\, material and living
  costs (a 10 percent personal contribution is automatically deducted by th
 e Mondriaan Fund)\; studio\, living space and Inside-Out Art Museum suppor
 t are paid directly by the Mondriaan Fund. For a selected duo the total is
  increased proportionally to cover the second applicant's travel and accom
 modation. Contribution for Caribbean-based residents can be increased for 
 higher travel costs. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months: 1 March 
 to 30 May 2027 (flexible start date\, set by IOAM in consultation with the
  resident)\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/subsidie-aanvragen/regel
